  "behavior": [
    "AccEngine previously reserved aligned_size(size)+align-4 for every typed allocation, consuming36/44 arena bytes for measured native32/40 ordered nodes even when their actual cursor was already aligned.",
    "Actual block cursor determines the downward aligned start and exact byte reservation. Last-block preference, oversize branch and15-previous-block scan retain native ordering for matching geometries; raw four-byte reservations still match native.",
    "Fresh blocks rely on raw_heap Layout alignment16 and a16-byte payload header offset, not observed platform addresses. Additional capacity above native size is needed only when the requested alignment exceeds16; actual consumption always uses the checked cursor after allocation.",
    "No alignment guarantee is weakened. Cursor residues are tested for align8/16/32/64/256, including misaligned native raw geometries where Rust deliberately pads. Filled-block/new-block/previous-block/oversize allocation and release rows match native exactly when aligned.",
    "Allocations and counts stay inside the existing single engine mutex. Incremental allocation+lease paths and f51a93dc reset-race correction are unchanged. Existing lease tests plus concurrent typed-owner and partial-constructor-panic tests pass.",
    "A separate pre-existing Rust ownership bug is repaired: valid typed interior addresses beyond native findBlock's two-key window, and zero-byte owned endpoints, previously failed lookup silently, retaining count/block until arena destruction. Both deterministic tests failed before and now release correctly.",
    "Owned release first validates native lookup against actual allocation bounds, then scans retained blocks only on a miss. Bounds come from the existing raw_heap header, with no duplicate owner registry or fabricated graph; raw Free preserves native lookup/error behavior.",
    "The ordered canonical test helper now asserts measured native32/40 cursor consumption. Old committed receipts stay historical. Controlled old-engine baselines fail all6 new reservation tests and both strengthened ordered node assertions; old owned release fails2 of3 focused tests."
  ],
