  "adaptations_and_remaining_gaps": [
    "Native raw AccAllocator promises only4-byte alignment. Typed geometries requiring padding intentionally reserve additional bytes; arbitrary typed alignment histories are not native raw byte parity. Exact32/40 closure concerns the measured already-aligned ordered node geometries.",
    "Over-aligned fresh blocks may reserve extra total capacity to guarantee a suitable start. Raw heap headers, generic physical heap footprint, allocation callbacks and native memory-manager configuration are not matched by these cursor measurements.",
    "Public raw Free/check_free/find_block retain native two-key lookup failures. Safe owners use additional actual-extent lookup so accepted Rust layouts remain deallocatable; that fallback is an explicit Rust ownership adaptation, not a change to the native raw API.",
    "Exceptional owned-release lookup is linear in live blocks. Normal native lookup remains first; no performance parity or lock-free behavior is claimed.",
    "The76-row callable audit distinguishes existing adapters, deleted methods, partial metadata wrappers and missing protected operations. It is a navigation/checklist artifact, not compiler-body proof or automatic global API closure. RTTI adapters are referenced but not newly exercised here.",
    "Native overflow, zero-size raw endpoint errors, OOM reporting, subclass callbacks and direct mutable protected block fields remain scoped. No whole allocator ABI equivalence or full kernel API/test parity is claimed."
  ]
